cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the report, please cite it as below."
title: "Intelligent Network Intrusion Detection System Using Machine Learning: an autoencoder-augmented stacked ensemble with novelty-aware stacking"
authors:
  - family-names: Majhi
    given-names: Sayan
type: software
version: "2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-12"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SayanMajhi/Intelligent-Network-Intrusion-Detection-System"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - intrusion detection
  - NSL-KDD
  - anomaly detection
  - autoencoder
  - stacked ensemble
abstract: >-
  A network intrusion detector for NSL-KDD connection records. Benign-only
  autoencoders provide anomaly features (a single reconstruction error or a
  31-dimensional per-subspace error profile) to a stacked ensemble of tree
  learners whose logistic meta-learner is trained on out-of-fold predictions
  from both stratified folds and folds that hold out whole attack types. On
  KDDTest+ the binary detector reaches 86.52% accuracy and detects 79.63% of
  records from attack types absent from training.
